AHH -- n-th map in the Aramova-Herzog-Hibi resolution
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        AHH(n, I)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * I, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, representing the n-th
        differential of the Aramova-Herzog-Hibi resolution

Description
===========

Returns the n-th map in the squarefree analogue of the Eliahou-Kervaire
resolution, due to Aramova, Herzog, and Hibi [AHH].

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                   |
|                                     |
|o1 = R                               |
|                                     |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                  |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal(x*y, x*z, y*z)|
|                                     |
|o2 = monomialIdeal (x*y, x*z, y*z)   |
|                                     |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R              |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : AHH(0, I)                       |
|                                     |
|o3 = | xy xz yz |                    |
|                                     |
|             1      3                |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                 |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : AHH(2, I)                       |
|                                     |
|o4 = 0                               |
|                                     |
|             2                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- 0                 |
+-------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Does not verify squarefree stability of I; use *note isSQStable: isSQStable,.

See also
========

  * *note isSQStable: isSQStable, -- test whether a squarefree monomial ideal
    is squarefree stable
  * *note AHHResolution: AHHResolution, -- Aramova-Herzog-Hibi minimal free
    resolution of a squarefree-stable ideal
  * *note EK: EK, -- n-th map in the Eliahou-Kervaire resolution

Ways to use AHH:
================

  * "AHH(ZZ,MonomialIdeal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note AHH: AHH, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

