cartanEilenbergResolution -- Computes free resolution of a ChainComplex
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        m = cartanEilenbergResolution C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note chain complex: (OldChainComplexes)ChainComplex,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note LengthLimit: cartanEilenbergResolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLengthLimit
        =>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity, How many steps to
        compute
  * Outputs:
      * m, a *note chain complex map: (OldChainComplexes)ChainComplexMap,,
        surjective quasi-isomorphism from a free ChainComplex

Description
===========

Uses a different algorithm than resolutionOfChainComplex, often slower and less
nearly minimal, to compute a free resolution of a chain complex. See
resolutionOfChainComplex for an example.

See also
========

  * *note resolutionOfChainComplex: resolutionOfChainComplex, -- free
    resolution of a chain complex

Ways to use cartanEilenbergResolution:
======================================

  * "cartanEilenbergResolution(ChainComplex)"

