EK -- n-th map in the Eliahou-Kervaire resolution
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        EK(n, I)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * I, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, representing the n-th
        differential of the Eliahou-Kervaire resolution

Description
===========

Returns the n-th map in the Eliahou-Kervaire resolution of S/I, following the
formulas in [EK]. For n == 0 this is just the generator matrix gens I. The
function does not check whether I is stable; on a non-stable ideal the
resulting complex may not be a resolution.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                        |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal(x^2, x*y, y^2, y*z)|
|                                          |
|                     2        2           |
|o2 = monomialIdeal (x , x*y, y , y*z)     |
|                                          |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : EK(0, I)                             |
|                                          |
|o3 = | x2 xy y2 yz |                      |
|                                          |
|             1      4                     |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                      |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : EK(2, I)                             |
|                                          |
|o4 = {3} | 0  |                           |
|     {3} | z  |                           |
|     {3} | -y |                           |
|     {3} | x  |                           |
|                                          |
|             4      1                     |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                      |
+------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Does not verify stability of I; use *note isStable: isStable, to check.

See also
========

  * *note isStable: isStable, -- test whether a monomial ideal is stable
  * *note EKResolution: EKResolution, -- Eliahou-Kervaire minimal free
    resolution of a stable monomial ideal
  * *note AHH: AHH, -- n-th map in the Aramova-Herzog-Hibi resolution

Ways to use EK:
===============

  * "EK(ZZ,MonomialIdeal)"

