resolution(ChainComplex) -- Resolves a ChainComplex.
****************************************************

  * Function: *note resolution: (OldChainComplexes)resolution,
  * Usage: 
        resolution C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note chain complex: (OldChainComplexes)ChainComplex,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeLimit: (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value null,
      * *note FastNonminimal: (OldChainComplexes)FastNonminimal, => ...,
        default value false,
      * *note HardDegreeLimit:
        (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmHardDegreeLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => ..., default value {},
      * *note LengthLimit: (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmLengthLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
      * *note PairLimit: (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmPairLimit
        =>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
      * ParallelizeByDegree (missing documentation) => ..., default value
        false,
      * *note SortStrategy: (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmSortStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value 0,
      * *note StopBeforeComputation:
        (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStopBeforeComputation=>_pd_
        pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value false,
      * *note Strategy: (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_
        pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value null,
      * *note SyzygyLimit: (OldChainComplexes)resolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_
        cmSyzygyLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
  * Outputs:
      * ChainComplex

Description
===========

Returns a surjective ChainComplexMap that is a quasi-isomorphism from a
(generally non-minimal) ChainComplex of free modules. resolution C is the same
as resolutionOfChainComplex C. The quasi-isomorphism is computed by the method
of iterated mapping cones. (For the computation of the Cartan-Eilenberg
resolution, which is usually slower and results in a larger complex, use
cartanEilenbergResolution C
+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[a..d]                         |
|                                                |
|o1 = R                                          |
|                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                             |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,2,3})          |
|                                                |
|             2                    2             |
|o2 = ideal (c  - b*d, b*c - a*d, b  - a*c)      |
|                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = koszulComplex(ideal vars R) ** (R^1/I);|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : m = res C;                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isQuasiIsomorphism m                       |
|                                                |
|o5 = true                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : betti source m                             |
|                                                |
|            0 1  2  3  4  5 6                   |
|o6 = total: 1 7 20 30 25 11 2                   |
|         0: 1 4  6  4  1  . .                   |
|         1: . 3 14 26 24 11 2                   |
|                                                |
|o6 : BettiTally                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
