taylor -- Gives the nth differential in the Taylor resolution of a monomial ideal I.
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        T = taylor(n,I)
  * Inputs:
      * n, 
      * I, 
  * Outputs:
      * T, the nth differential in the Taylor Resolution of I.

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b]                   |
|                                       |
|o1 = R                                 |
|                                       |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal (ideal vars R)^3|
|                                       |
|                     3   2      2   3  |
|o2 = monomialIdeal (a , a b, a*b , b ) |
|                                       |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R                |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : T2 = taylor(2,I)                  |
|                                       |
|o3 = {3} | -b -b2 0  -b3 0   0  |      |
|     {3} | a  0   -b 0   -b2 0  |      |
|     {3} | 0  a2  a  0   0   -b |      |
|     {3} | 0  0   0  a3  a2  a  |      |
|                                       |
|             4      6                  |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                   |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : T3 = taylor(3,I)                  |
|                                       |
|o4 = {4} | b  b2 0  0  |               |
|     {5} | -1 0  b  0  |               |
|     {4} | a  0  0  b  |               |
|     {6} | 0  -1 -1 0  |               |
|     {5} | 0  a  0  -1 |               |
|     {4} | 0  0  a2 a  |               |
|                                       |
|             6      4                  |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                   |
+---------------------------------------+

